1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:18,000
In Guatemala, digital identity must work even when institutions, aid programs, or employer portals leak personal data. ZPK Digital ID is a local-first Android wallet for that reality.

2
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:50,000
The submitted app uses synthetic data only. A citizen enters a test CUI, and ZPK registers a pseudonymous identity on the device. The raw CUI is not sent to a server.

3
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:20,000
The local agent checks risk, chooses a privacy route, and creates a DID-style document, an HMAC-signed recovery credential, selective disclosure claims, and a 15-minute consent proof.

4
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:55,000
For richer reasoning, ZPK has a hosted Gemma 4 mode verified with gemma-4-31b-it. The prompt receives redacted facts, not the raw CUI.

5
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:20,000
The app also integrates Cactus local inference evidence, ML Kit AICore fail-closed fallback, and a Gemma 4 adaptation pipeline with SFT data, teacher traces, and GRPO rewards.

6
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:50,000
This is not a production government identity system. It is an offline testbed for safer national digital identity in Guatemala and a pattern that can extend across Latin America.
